question:
Show that $f(x) = 2e^{-2x}, 0 \le x < \infty$ represents probability density function for a random variable $x$. Calculate:
(i) $P(x \le 3)$;
(ii) $P(x \ge 2)$.

For a Binomial distribution with $6$ trials and $p = 0.125$, find the probability that:
(i) all six trials are successful;
(ii) at most two trials are successful;
(iii) none of the trials is successful.

The average birth in a certain community is $5$ per day; find the probability that in a certain day:
(i) there will be $2$ births;
(ii) at least $3$ births.

Two dice are tossed once. What is the probability that the product of the outcome is:
(i) less than $7$;
(ii) even;
(iii) odd?
